		{
			"id": "115169782162700501",
			"parentId": "115169768783455820",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/115169782162700501",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-08T17:10:12.394Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@localnerve\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>localnerve</span></a></span> I’m not sure this would fix it? I think <a href=\"https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publish</span><span class=\"invisible\">ers</span></a> is the new thing that might help prevent bad publishes from other workflows <a href=\"https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publish</span><span class=\"invisible\">ers</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115169836927682739",
			"parentId": "115169782162700501",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@localnerve/115169836842047584",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Grant",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@localnerve",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/115/141/968/680/223/545/original/1d8ffc7eeafe91eb.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-08T17:24:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>This is the workflow we use, yes? I see 11ty has this also. This, combined with the workflow and socket.dev integration is what stopped me at ~10:20am this morning.</p><p>It won't fix everything, no.</p><p>The error-ex case today, by examining the delta between the source code on github and the package delivered by npmjs, indicates ppl (or agents acting on their behalf) are publishing directly, injecting code. The packages have code different from the repo, and pub provenance eliminates that.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115169878234247292",
			"parentId": "115169836927682739",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/115169878234247292",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-08T17:34:38.329Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@localnerve\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>localnerve</span></a></span> ah, yeah — for sure. I just mean that packages using provenance aren’t *required* to use provenance to publish (which was an interesting design decision)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115169933404689789",
			"parentId": "115169878234247292",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@localnerve/115169933364426393",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Grant",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@localnerve",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/115/141/968/680/223/545/original/1d8ffc7eeafe91eb.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-08T17:48:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>I think we're quickly heading to a point where it will be a requirement. </p><p>Ppl doing strategic forks (fork, contribute, but republish with provenance) will help drive this. Ppl with bigger budgets have to drive this for bigger packages. </p><p>I cant believe packages like <a href=\"https://mastodon.social/tags/jest\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>jest</span></a> have the dep supply chain they have. That's major. </p><p>We gotta get better.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
